{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Combined Heat Transfer Modes.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Combined Heat Transfer Modes.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"combined heat transfer modes combined heat transfer modes","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Combined Heat Transfer Modes.md","fileName":"Combined Heat Transfer Modes.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Combined Heat Transfer Modes","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-14 00:55\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Conduction Convection and Radiation]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Conduction Convection and Radiation","Energy Conservation in Thermal Continua","Conjugate Heat Transfer Coupling","cosmolheattransfermodels.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Combined Heat Transfer Modes.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Combined Heat Transfer Modes.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"combined heat transfer modes combined heat transfer modes","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Combined Heat Transfer Modes.md","fileName":"Combined Heat Transfer Modes.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Combined Heat Transfer Modes","heading":"Combined Heat Transfer Modes","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Practical thermal systems commonly conduct energy through solids, convect it through adjacent fluids, and radiate it between exposed surfaces at the same time. All three mechanisms share temperature difference as a driver but use different constitutive relations and geometric information.\n\nTheir contributions meet in one [[Energy Conservation in Thermal Continua|energy balance]]. A reduced model may replace fluid motion or radiation with boundary coefficients, while a [[Conjugate Heat Transfer Coupling|multiphysics model]] resolves interacting solid, fluid, and radiative fields when those approximations are insufficient.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Conduction Convection and Radiation","Energy Conservation in Thermal Continua","Conjugate Heat Transfer Coupling","cosmolheattransfermodels.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Combined Heat Transfer Modes.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Combined Heat Transfer Modes.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"combined heat transfer modes combined heat transfer modes","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Combined Heat Transfer Modes.md","fileName":"Combined Heat Transfer Modes.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Combined Heat Transfer Modes","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[cosmolheattransfermodels.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Conduction Convection and Radiation","Energy Conservation in Thermal Continua","Conjugate Heat Transfer Coupling","cosmolheattransfermodels.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}